  "body": "Normally a blob: URL is same-origin with the document that created it.\r\n\r\nBut if that document has a unique origin, per https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-origin the blob: URL will have a _different_ unique origin.  This is pretty unexpected.  I'm not even sure whether it matches implementations.  It definitely doesn't match Gecko's: the origin of a blob: URL in Gecko is the same as the origin of the document that would be created from the blob: URL; see https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2759 for details.",
